Vo_jnh6weLpC_OsvqMsqcqh2q1UZRgXN0g/viewform?usp=dialog)**\nRSVP on Meetup does **not** book you on this trip.\n\nCheers!\nFawn\n\n*The Travel Agent Next Door (TTAND)*\n*1003 - 55 York St. Toronto ON M5J 1R7*\nTel: 416-367-8264 Ext. 4620\n***TICO*** *Reg. #50021282*","startDate":"2026-10-16T10:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Pearson International Airport","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"M9HC+WJ Mississauga, Ontario, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Shared Tables - Solo Travel Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sharedtables-solotraveltoronto/"},"performer":"Shared Tables - Solo Travel Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🏕️ 3 Days, 6 Spots: Algonquin Park Awaits","url":"https://www.meetup.com/highparkhikingclub/events/316155894/","description":"Get your boots ready—we’re heading into the heart of [Algonquin Provincial Park](https://www.ontarioparks.ca/park/algonquin) for a 3-day backcountry hiking extravaganza.\n\nExpect stunning views, crisp forest air, brilliant colors and three full days of asking each other, *\"Does anyone know which way is North?\"*\n**The Catch:**\n\n* **Cap:** Strictly limited to **6 hikers** (because 7 is a crowd, and 8 requires a larger campfire circle). No camping just glamping in a hotel.\n* **Duration:** 3 days of pure trail bliss.\n* **Date:** October 16-18. That’s Friday to Sunday\n* **Details:** Top secret for now. Trail maps, packing lists, and more will drop as soon as you lock in your spot.\n\nFirst 6 to RSVP by September 14th get a ticket to the trail.\nHit reply to claim your spot before the bears beat you to it on this luxury autumn trek 🌲🥾 🍂","startDate":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"High Park Hiking Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/highparkhikingclub/"},"performer":"High Park Hiking Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"TEA AND TOUR AT THE LEGISLATIVE ASSEMBLY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-seniors-social-club/events/314908950/","description":"Let's enjoy some tea, crumpets, history, art and culture OCTOBER 16TH at Ontario's Parliament building. We will experience a tour and tea between 2 - 4 o'clock in the afternoon. **THIS EVENT IS BOOKED MONTHS IN ADVANCE, SO PLEASE PURCHASE YOUR TICKET ASAP, FOR THE 2-4 PM SLOT, TO BE SURE YOU GAIN ENTRANCE FOR THIS DAY. PLEASE ARRIVE 15 MINUTES EARLY.**\n\n**WHERE: ONTARIO LEGISLATIVE BUILDING**\n111 Wellesley Street West, just north of University Avenue and College Street\n**COST:** $45.00\n[Find your tour or webinar | Legislative Assembly of Ontario](https://www.ola.org/en/visit-learn/tours)\nFind tea and tour and hit availability. Go to the OCTOBER calendar and the 16TH day is the only day marked in green. Hit this and continue your booking...\n**BUY YOUR TICKET IMMEIDIATELY at this link. When you have booked your seat please submit your RSVP.**\n\nSUBWAY STOP IS QUEEN'S PARK STATION\nYOU MUST ARRIVE 15 MINUTES PRIOR TO THE START OF THE EVENT TO FACILITATE THE SECURITY SCREENING PROCESS.\n\n**YOU MUST PRESENT A PIECE OF GOVERNMENT- ISSUED PHOTO ID** TO ENTER THE BUILDING. ALL VISITORS MUST PASS THROUGH AN AIRPORT-STYLE SECURITY SCREEN TO ENTER THE LEGISLATIVE BUILDING.","startDate":"2026-10-16T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"111 Wellesley St W","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"111 Wellesley St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Seniors Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-seniors-social-club/"},"performer":"Toronto Seniors Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"20th Anniversary of Cask Days","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316173138/","description":"## 20 Years of Cask Days\n\nCalling all members - from the O.G. to the newest one - come join us for some fine beer.\n\n**Cask Days** is a celebration of cask-conditioned beer, naturally carbonated, unfiltered and served straight from the cask. Once tapped, it has only a few days to be enjoyed in its prime. We call them Cask Days.\nJoin us October 16–18, 2026, at [282 Campbell Ave](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bt3PLEYsF8TtVi2J7)., the future home of [Bottega Volo’s](http://bottegavolo.com/) second location. The 20th edition will feature 100+ casks from breweries across Canada, natural wine, great food and music. It all began on the patio of [Bar Volo](http://barvolo.com/) in 2005.\n\nYour Co-Organizers have purchased tickets for Session 2 Friday October 16, 2026 from 5 - 9 p.m. - I have included the ticket information below. They have posted that they are already over 50% sold and they only went on sale August 11, 2026.\n\nPlease visit their website for more information if needed: [https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets](https://caskdays.com/cask-days#tickets)\n\nFriday, October 16, 2026\n\n***Session 2: **5:00 pm - 9:00 pm\n\nOne 4-hour session\n4 food and drink tokens\nOfficial Cask Days 2026 mug\n100+ cask-conditioned ales\n19+ with government-issued ID\nLimited to 500 guests\n[282 Campbell Ave.](https://maps.app.goo.gl/Bvxpgwy3B2dAcnKcA) (Clock Factory Building)\n$50\n- tax & processing fees\n\nLink to buy tickets: [https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival](https://cask-days.bloomtickets.ca/event/2120?20thAnnualCaskDaysBeerFestival)\n\nIf you can't go to Session 2 please try and attend one of the other sessions as it really is an experience.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\n## CASK AVAILABILITY\n\nCask ale waits for no one. Once tapped, each cask has only a few glorious days at its best—and when it’s gone, it’s gone. We’ll have just one cask of each beer, so if something special has caught your eye, book an earlier session and get to it before the crowd does.\n\n## SERVINGS & GLASSWARE\n\nCask Days is a tasting journey, so every beer is poured in a 5 oz serving. Most pours cost one token, while specialty and stronger ales cost two. Your official Cask Days 2026 mug is included with your ticket and is yours to keep and reuse throughout the festival.\n\n## FOOD & DRINK TOKENS\n\nTokens are your festival currency, good for cask ales and food at every session. Each token is worth $3.75 plus tax, and Session 1–4 tickets include 4x tokens to get you started. Need more? Tokens will be available for purchase at the event. Tokens are non-refundable.\n\nLINEUP\nFeaturing cask-ales from…\n\n#### ONTARIO All My Friends • Amsterdam • AURUM• Badlands • Bellwoods • Beyond the Pale • Bickford • Black Lab • Blood Brothers • Bobcaygeon • Burdock • C’est What Durham • Clifford • Common Good • Conjure • Dominion City • Fairweather • Ferm Farm • Fine Balance • Godspeed • Granite • Great Lakes • Indie Alehouse • Left Field • Lovebird • Matron • McGrath • Muddy York • Nickel Brook • Paradise Grapevine • Rainhard • Revel Cider • Rorschach • Rouge River • Short Finger • Silversmith • Slake • Something in the Water • Steadfast • Third Moon • Tooth and Nail • Town • TRUE HISTORY• Two Loons • Volo • Wellington • Willibald\n\n#### QUEBEC • 5e Baron • Albion • Dieu du Ciel! • Dunham • Hopfenstark • Isle de Garde • Mellön • Messorem • WILLS • NOVA SCOTIA • Big Spruce • Boxing Rock • North • Propeller • Schoolhouse • Stillwell • Tatamagouche • ALBERTA • Ale Architect • Annex Ale Project • Bent Stick • Blind Enthusiasm • Blindman • Cabin • Dandy • The Establishment • BRITISH COLUMBIA • Four Winds • Luppolo • Slow Hand • Small Gods • Superflux • Temporal Artisan Ales\n\n[CASK LIST COMING SOON!](https://caskdays.com/cask-days)\n\n## WHAT IS CASK ALE?\n\nBefore metal kegs, CO₂, and refrigeration, beer was served as cask-conditioned ale. Unlike most beer, cask ale continues fermenting in the cask until just before it's poured, creating its naturally gentle carbonation. Before serving, the cask is vented to release excess gas and the yeast settles to the bottom. The result is a beer that's lightly carbonated, served at cellar temperature, and exceptionally fresh, with vibrant flavour and character. Once tapped, a cask is best enjoyed within just a few days.** We call those days, Cask Days.**\n\nTheir website has a lot of FAQ's.\n\nHope to see a lot of members there.","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Cask Days Beer Festival","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"282 Campbell Ave. (Clock Factory Building), Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316727509/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍻 🍺 DRINKS AFTER WORK","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-haus-meetup/events/316727561/","description":"Drinks after work!","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Cactus Club","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"77 Adelaide St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"SOCIAL HAUS - TORONTO","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-haus-meetup/"},"performer":"SOCIAL HAUS - TORONTO"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Gayme Night @ LVLUP GAMES","url":"https://www.meetup.com/m-b-g-u/events/316727532/","description":"Join us for a Gayme Night where you can meet other LGBTQIA2S+ people and allies. Socialize, play board games, and unwind from a weeks worth of work for all board game experience levels!\n\n⌛**Time**: 5 PM - 8 PM\n💰 **Price**: $8.00 + tax\n\nAllies are welcomed :)\n\nTickets may be purchased in advance through lvlupgames.ca (https://lvlupgames.ca/products/gayme-night-lgbtqia2splus-community-game-night)","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"LVLUP GAMES","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"833 Westlock Rd Unit #9, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Mississauga Board Gamers United","url":"https://www.meetup.com/m-b-g-u/"},"performer":"Mississauga Board Gamers United"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Seaton Trail","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/events/316622838/","description":"**I’m organizing a fall hike at Seaton Trail in Pickering October 16, at 5 30 p.m.**\n\n**We’ll aim for an 8–10 km hike, taking approximately 3–4 hours at a moderate pace, with breaks to enjoy the fall colours and take pictures.**\n\n**It should be a lovely opportunity to enjoy nature, get some exercise and meet new people.**\n\n**Bring comfortable hiking shoes, water and snacks. Let me know if you’d like to join!**","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Whitevale Community Centre","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Pickering","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"405 Whitevale Rd, Pickering, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Move With Intention","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-bonfires-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Move With Intention"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🐾 Give Back: TNR Cat Rescue Volunteer Day","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316773228/","description":"Please read the details before RSVPing.\n\n🐾 Time to give back, guys\n\nWe’ve partnered with a non-profit animal rescue group to support a TNR (Trap-Neuter-Return) campaign in Scarborough, near 75 Birchmount Ave.\n\nWe’re looking for volunteers to help with\n\n1. 🪤 Setting up traps at designated locations\n2. 🚗 Transporting cats to/from the clinic\n3. 🐱 Feeding cats at designated locations\n\nSome activities require access to your own vehicle, while others simply require your time and willingness to help.\n\nEvery little bit helps, and the cats definitely need us. ❤️?\n\nAnyone allergic to cats, furs or anything related to animals, please do not signup\n\nYou participate this in this event at your own risk. Organizers of this meetup or anyone who is part of this campaign isn't responsible for any untoward incident during your participation in this event .","startDate":"2026-10-16T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Scarborough Gardens Arena","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"75 Birchmount Road, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎬Movie: Whalefall -  Food & Drinks after the movie 🍿!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316155632/","description":"🎬 Let’s Go to the Movies (and Actually Talk… or Not)\n\nWhether you're a film nerd, popcorn enthusiast, or just looking for a chill night out with interesting people — this one's for you.\n\nWe’re heading out to see a movie together, then grabbing food or drinks after. If the film's great (or terrible), we’ll probably talk about it forever. If it’s just okay, we’ll talk about it for 10 minutes and move on to everything else — books, dating apps, weird dreams, how Toronto keeps getting more expensive, etc.\n\nThe vibe is relaxed, friendly, and not too serious. No film degree needed. No icebreakers. No pressure to “perform.” Just come enjoy the film, connect with some thoughtful people, and see where the night goes Click here to watch trailer!\n\n🎞️ **Movie Title + Trailer:** [\\[Click here to watch trailer!\\]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=67ho3OxCmmM)\n\n📖 **📖 Plot Summary:** Centering on a scuba diver in search of his deceased father’s remains who gets swallowed by an 80-foot, 60-ton sperm whale and has only one hour to escape before his oxygen runs out. After giving up on life, the young man is surprised to find a reason to live in the most dangerous and unlikely of places.\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ **Event Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Time:** 6:00 PM (Final time + theatre announced Tuesday of event week)\n🎬 **Movie Start Time:** TBA\n⏱️ **Runtime:** TBA\n📌 **Meetup Spot:** To be confirmed (based on theatre)\n🎟️ **Cost:**\n\n* **$11.50** for *CineClub* members\n* **$16.00** regular admission\n👉 You are responsible for buying your own ticket.\n\n**🪑 Reserved Seating:**\nYou must buy your ticket *before* signing up. You'll be asked where you're sitting so we can all sit together! However, members are welcome to sit anywhere that works for them.\n🎫 Buy your ticket here: [https://www.cineplex.com](https://www.cineplex.com)\n📍🪑 **Where I will be sitting:**\n\n🍿 **After the Movie:**\nYes, we’re heading out after! It’s not just a movie night — it’s a social night. Let's talk, laugh, and dissect every plot twist.\n\n***\n\n### ✅ **Before You Sign Up**\n\n* Please **buy your ticket first** — seating is limited!\n* When signing up, let us know your **seat number** so we can try to group everyone together.\n* You can still sign up or just **show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it — we’re flexible!\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)\n🎟️ **Join Cineplex’s CineClub for discounts**: [https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub](https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub)\n🎁 **Get your SCENE Card** for free movies and points: [https://www.scene.ca](https://www.scene.ca)\n\n***\n\n### 🎥 **A Quick Word About Movie Etiquette**\n\nWe love a great film experience. Please:\n\n* Turn off your phone\n* Don’t talk during the movie\n* Be respectful of others\n\nRepeat offenders will be removed from the group — we take our cinema seriously (but with snacks).\n\n***\n\n### 👥 **About the Group**\n\nThis event is open to everyone — single, not single, shy, social, new in town or a long-time local. We're a group for people who love movies *and* making real connections. We also do walks, hikes, restaurants, arts & culture — come be part of it!\n🎬 **Organized by:** Mathew\n📧 Questions? Reach out: **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cuddle Club - platonic body nourishing.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316727876/","description":"**CUDDLE CLUB.**\n**Have you tried that?**\n\n**In Amsterdam cuddle events are sold out quickly. Even few different Cuddle clubs are happening at the same day. It's so popular there.**\n\n**In Toronto there** **is** **nearly no Cuddle clubs yet.**\n**But we are doing that.**\n**Join our tantric group and leave a message in comments if you wanna join the waiting list.**\n**T.me/TorontoTantra**\n**___**\n**About this event**\n**• What is the cuddle club?**\n\n**It’s a cozy evening to experience how deeply nourishing it can feel to be held, without any romantic or sexual expectations. A space where people can come together to share love and touch. We cuddle platonically, the way you’d hold a child or a kitten.**\n\n**• What will we be doing?**\n\n**Facilitator will guide you through some gentle exercises to help you unwind after your day, soften into your body, and calm your nervous system. We aim to make you feel safe in your own body, which can help you connect with others.**\n\n**• Cuddle puddle perfection**\n\n**Everything is by invitation, but we will guide you into a beautifully structured cuddle puddle. It is a very comfortable, welcoming way of cuddling where you are held and touched by multiple people at the same time. Chances are you’ll float home afterwards, high on oxytocin.**\n\n**• Important terms & agreements:**\n1. **Keep it platonic: we cuddle without romantic or sexual expectations or escalations**\n1. **Take care of yourself and others: communicate and respect boundaries**\n1. **Be here fully: This is a sober space. No drugs, no alcohol. No phones.**\n\n**Details in telegram group:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n**Regular Ticket — $50 CAD**\n**Early Bird Ticket — $35 CAD (If you register and pay before August 31).**\n**Supportive Ticket — $25 CAD (For students and people with low financial income).**\n**Combo — $60 CAD for 2 people (Bring a friend).**\n\n**Free participation.**\n**We want everyone to have an opportunity to participate. If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-16T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/4/6/e/highres_534817998.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/3/e/0/highres_535713760.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/a/a/3/highres_534351875.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/7/3/5/highres_535730997.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/9/f/4/highres_535655316.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/7/7/8/highres_508495160.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href=